    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d588">

                <pb facs="0888" n="878" xml:id="pg878"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by General Chou
                            En-lai to General Marshall
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">MM 201</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-10-12">October 12, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear General Marshall</hi>: We have not received any
                    report as to which troops conducted the incident at Hsin-Ho. Upon reading your
                    memorandum OSE 505<anchor n="70" xml:id="d588-f1"/> addressed to General Chou
                    En-lai, I immediately dispatched a message to Yenan authorities, asking them to
                    probe and clarify if the Communist forces near by the town did make the acts, as
                    you asserted in the memorandum. I will let you know of the result, as soon as
                    any reply is received.</p>
                <closer>For General Chou En-lai: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tung Pi-Wu</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d588-f1" n="70" xml:id="d588-f1-content">
